hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1479","Issa bin Abi Harb told us, Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, Abu Jafar al-Razi told us, Husayn bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Ibn Umm Maktum, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, received the people during the evening prayer, and he said: “I was about to come Those who neglect this prayer, I will burn their houses.” Then Ibn Umm Maktoum got up and said: O Messenger of God, you know what is wrong with me. And I have no leader. He said: “Do you hear the Iqama?” He said: Yes, he said: “Bring it,” and he did not give him permission. Abu Bakr said: This word: And I have no leader, in it is a summary. He wanted my knowledge, and there is no leader who follows me, like the report of Abu Razin, on the authority of Ibn Umm Muffled"
"1480","Nasr bin Marzuq narrated to us, Asad narrated to us, Shayban Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Abi Al-Najjoud, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Ibn Umm Maktoum, narrated by Muhammad bin Al-Hasan bin Tasnim, narrated by Muhammad, meaning Ibn Bakr, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Razin, On the authority of Abdullah bin Umm Maktoum, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, I am an old man with blind eyes and a vast house, and I have a leader, so he does not keep me company. So do I have someone? A license? He said: “Do you hear the call?” He said: Yes. He said: “I can find no concession for you.”"
